{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"a5b9095562d91d1a23014bb681dddf7f9f75df2a35e796434312ea1c8fe0c2cd","digest":{"component_or_area":"plan review manifest byte-equality tests","key_entities":["src/rebar/llm/plan_review/manifest.py:497","src/rebar/_signing_manifest.py:_gate_commit_sha","tests/unit/test_plan_review.py::test_manifest_file_scope_contract_preserves_legacy_bytes","tests/unit/test_plan_material_pins.py::test_no_pins_preserves_legacy_manifest_bytes","tests/unit/test_gate_engine_cutover.py::test_manifest_is_deterministic_and_path_independent","rebar.signing.gate_code_version","rebar.signing","build_manifest"],"problem_keywords":["flaky test","byte-equality","git dirty-state","xdist","manifest","non-deterministic"],"propositions":["Manifest byte-equality tests fail flakily under pytest-xdist because gate_code_version() shells git status --porcelain on each call, causing -dirty suffix to flip between two build_manifest calls when concurrent workers touch the checkout.","Two test functions compare separately-built manifests without pinning gate_code_version: test_manifest_file_scope_contract_preserves_legacy_bytes and test_manifest_is_deterministic_and_path_independent.","Pinning rebar.signing.gate_code_version via monkeypatch (the pattern already used in test_no_pins_preserves_legacy_manifest_bytes) eliminates the race and makes equality assertions stable.","All manifest byte-equality tests in the repo must pin gate_code_version to prevent concurrent git-state changes from flipping provenance metadata between test calls."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timesta